          <p>
            Weigh the job honestly. A large gravel lot full of mature perennials is a herbicide job, and trying to hand pull it is a recipe for a sore back and the same weeds next year. Ten dandelions in a healthy lawn are a hand-tool job. Using the least product that solves the problem saves money and keeps the yard safer for everyone who walks on it.
          </p>

          <p>
            Cleanup matters too. Clippings and pulled weeds left on walks scatter seed back into cracks, so a quick pass with a <a href="/best-cordless-leaf-blower/">cordless leaf blower</a> after weeding or mowing keeps hard surfaces clean and gives new weeds fewer places to start.
          </p>
