        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the chemistry that fits the job. A selective product such as Tenacity for weeds in a lawn, a systemic concentrate for clearing beds and fence lines to the roots, a residual vegetation killer only for ground that should stay bare and has no tree roots beneath it, and a pre-emergent such as Preen once beds are already clean.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then let the label run the job: the rate, the timing, the rainfast window, the protective gear and how long pets stay off. Spray only the weed, never the pavement around it, and choose a calm, dry morning. Do that and a single bottle goes further, works better and stays out of the storm drain.
          </p>
